# zig-only
# `editor.format_external` with nothing in `.formatters` falls back to
# the builtin table (`src/lsp/tools.zig`): a `.zig` buffer goes through
# `zig fmt --stdin` — on PATH wherever this suite runs — and the tool's
# stdout replaces the text as one edit, so the buffer turns dirty.
write a.zig "const  x=1;\n"
open a.zig
command editor.format_external
expect screen contains "formatted a.zig with zig"
expect screen contains "const x = 1;"
expect dirty true
